From a7634948f799895bf4e353b7c8d29c73de05d4e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 03:36:30 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 360/365] DOS-PORT: patch 0360 -- script VM slice 2: a threaded
 fast loop over the decoded stream (DOSAGS_VM=fast)

The loop that uses 0359's stream (docs/lab/VM-DESIGN.md 3, docs/lab/VM-SLICE2.md): one handler per
(opcode, operand variant), dispatched by GCC computed goto through a handler table, with
ip and this held in callee-saved registers across the dispatch (VM-SLICE0: checked in -S at the
project flags: every dispatch must stay "jmp *(%edi)"). CallScriptFunction enters it through
DosVmEnter(), which falls back to the untouched upstream Run() for a script that did not decode,
under the debugger, or when DOSAGS_VM is not fast. Any instruction without a handler of its own, and
every instruction in DOSAGS_VM=fastgeneric, runs through DosVmStep(): Run()'s own switch text,
transformed mechanically (Run()'s locals -> a frame struct), so the semantics are Run()'s.

Opt-in here (DOSAGS_VM=fast); 0365 makes it the default. Lab-only code is compiled only with
-DDOSAGS_VMTRACE (make AGS_RUNSTATS_DEF=-DDOSAGS_VMTRACE): a per-instruction trace digest folded
identically in Run() and the fast loop, and the statewit determinism witness (character/object/
global/script-data digests every 25 ticks, DOSAGS_WIT_PERTURB_TICK as its control).

Lab: trace and state digests EQUAL to legacy on MMD character select, AGS Quest (incl. restore),
seeded 5 Days and the MMD intro (26.7M instructions); MMD CS script event 9.311 -> 5.130 ms/tick at
fixed 40k cycles. 486, round F1b (same lab binary, legacy vs fast): MMD displayed 26.77 -> 86.94%,
script_vm 20.47 -> 12.70 ms/tick (1.61x).

