 //=============================================================================
 //
-// DOS-PORT patch 0359 -- script VM slice 1: decode each script once at load into an
-// index-parallel stream (docs/lab/VM-DESIGN.md 2.2-2.3), and check it.
+// DOS-PORT patch 0359 -- the script VM: decode each script once at load (slice 1) and run the
+// decoded stream in a threaded loop (slice 2). docs/lab/VM-DESIGN.md 2.2-2.10.
 //
-// Inert unless DOSAGS_VM is set: with DOSAGS_VM unset (or "legacy") ResolveImportFixups makes
-// one cached getenv() and nothing else, and no memory is allocated. Nothing executes the
-// decoded stream yet; ccInstance::Run() is untouched.
-//
-//   DOSAGS_VM=decode  decode every primary instance at load; one "vmdecode" log line each
-//   DOSAGS_VM=check   the same, then re-derive every instruction independently of the decoder
-//                     (its own walk over the ORIGINAL ccScript code, the legacy fixup text, field
-//                     by field RuntimeScriptValue comparison) and log a "vmcheck" line
+// DOSAGS_VM (read once):
+//   unset/legacy  nothing is decoded; ccInstance::Run() runs every script, as before
+//   decode        decode every primary instance at load and log it (nothing executes it)
+//   check         decode, then verify the stream against the bytecode (slice 1's gate)
+//   fast          decode; CallScriptFunction() runs eligible scripts in DosVmLoop()
+//   fastnofuse    the same as fast (slice 2 has no superinstructions yet)
+//   fastgeneric   decode; every instruction goes through DosVmStep(), the legacy-text stepper
+// DOSAGS_VM_CHECK=1 additionally runs the slice-1 check in any decoding mode.
 //
 // Layout (VM-DESIGN 2.2). For an instruction at pc with argc arguments:
-//   dcode[pc]          its handler kind: bits 0-7 the opcode as Run() executes it (the
-//                      CALLEXT->CALLAS rewrite included), bits 8-15 a variant (kVmV_*);
-//                      slice 2 maps kinds to handler label addresses
-//   dcode[pc+1+k]      argument k, pre-processed BY OPCODE:
-//                        register argument  -> reg * sizeof(RuntimeScriptValue)
-//                        jzi/jnzi/jmpi      -> word delta (arg + 2) when the target is an
-//                                              instruction start inside the code (variant 0),
-//                                              else the raw word (variant kVmV_Slow)
-//                        LITTOREG/WRITELIT argument 2, by its fixup type:
-//                          none / FUNCTION  -> the int (variant 0)
-//                          GLOBALDATA       -> &((ScriptVariable*)word)->RValue (kVmV_Gvar)
-//                          STRING           -> _strings + word (kVmV_Str)
-//                          IMPORT           -> the import INDEX, looked up at run time (kVmV_Imp)
-//                          STACK / other    -> raw word (kVmV_Slow: the generic stepper)
-//                        anything else      -> the raw word, exactly what Run() reads
-//   dcode[n..n+2]      zero padding
-// A script with an opcode >= CC_NUM_SCCMDS, an instruction running past the end, or a register
-// argument outside 0..CC_NUM_REGISTERS-1 is NOT decoded (decoded_ok = false): it would always
-// run the legacy Run(), keeping today's behaviour by construction.
+//   dcode[pc]       check/decode modes: its kind (bits 0-7 the opcode as Run() executes it,
+//                   bits 8-15 a variant kVmV_*); fast modes: the address of its handler label
+//   dcode[pc+1+k]   argument k, pre-processed BY OPCODE: a register -> reg*sizeof(RSV);
+//                   jzi/jnzi/jmpi -> (arg + 2) when the target is an instruction start inside the
+//                   code, else the raw word (variant kVmV_Slow); LITTOREG/WRITELIT argument 2 by
+//                   fixup: none/FUNCTION -> the int, GLOBALDATA -> &ScriptVariable::RValue,
+//                   STRING -> _strings + word, IMPORT -> the index (looked up at run time),
+//                   STACK/other -> raw (kVmV_Slow); anything else -> the raw word
+//   dcode[n..n+2]   zero
+// A script with an opcode >= CC_NUM_SCCMDS, an instruction running past the end or a register
+// argument outside 0..7 is not decoded and always runs the legacy Run().
+//
+// The fast loop keeps only ip and this live across dispatch; every other Run() local is in a
+// DosVmFrame. The member _pc is written before every call out of the loop and on every exit.
+// INSTF_ABORTED is tested at entry and after every handler that calls out (only engine code,
+// reached through a call out, can set it). Anything a native handler does not handle -- rare
+// opcodes, odd fixups, a precondition (stack space, register types) it would fail -- goes to
+// h_generic BEFORE any state is changed, and DosVmStep() executes that instruction with the text
+// of Run()'s own case (generated from cc_instance.cpp's switch, see DosVmStep).
